    <record id="slide_lesson_backgrounds_practice" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="name">Build a production background</field>
        <field name="channel_id" ref="slide_channel_backgrounds" />
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="is_preview" eval="False" />
        <field name="sequence">21</field>
        <field name="completion_time">0.75</field>
        <field
            name="description"
        >Hands-on exercise to design a background that serves the story.</field>
        <field
            name="html_content"
        ><![CDATA[
<h2>Build a production background</h2>
<p>Create a background that supports a short scene: establish the camera, the path of the character and the mood of the beat.</p>
<h3>Brief</h3>
<ol>
    <li>Pick a simple beat (arrival, chase or quiet wait).</li>
    <li>Block the shot with lines, shapes and a clear horizon.</li>
    <li>Lock a color script with one key light and one accent color.</li>
    <li>Paint in Photoshop at production resolution and leave space for animation.</li>
</ol>
<p>Deliver a layered PSD and a flattened preview. Adjust until the read works in grayscale.</p>
        ]]></field>
